{% comment %}
  blocks/_expert-quote-lead.liquid

  The words and the person who said them: a quotation mark, the quote, a line
  drawn down from it, and a portrait with a name and a role under it.

  ## One block, because it is one sentence

  The quote and the attribution were separate settings on the section before
  this, and separating them further into two blocks would have been worse than
  either. The connector line belongs to neither on its own — it exists only to
  carry the eye from the last word to the face — and a merchant who deletes
  "the expert" and is left with a section quoting nobody has been handed a way
  to break their own page. They are one claim, so they are one block.

  `sections/expert-quote.liquid` renders it with `content_for 'block'` rather
  than through `content_for 'blocks'`, so it is editable but cannot be dragged
  into the row of scattered pictures or deleted by accident. Same mechanism,
  same reason, as `sections/testimonials.liquid`'s intro panel.

  ## The mark is the theme's icon system, not a drawing kept here

  `snippets/icon.liquid` gained a `quote` glyph — the one from the design, at
  the proportions it was drawn with — so this block picks an icon the way every
  other block in the theme does: a source (none / icon / image), a name, a size
  off the shared ladder. A merchant who wants a star, a chat bubble or their own
  uploaded mark gets it without a code change, and a store that restyles its
  icons moves this one with them.

  ## The portrait is never an empty box

  With no upload, `snippets/image.liquid` draws a placeholder rather than
  leaving a hole where a face goes. The section is an endorsement; a merchant
  arranging one should be looking at the shape of a portrait while they decide
  whose it is.

  ## Two loops, and why they are on two different elements

  The ring turns and the portrait breathes. They are separate animations on
  separate elements on purpose: `rotate` on the ring and `scale` on the
  portrait would fight if they shared a box, and splitting them also means the
  dotted ring can spin while the face stays upright, which is the only version
  of this that does not look like a broken carousel.

  Both are decorative, both are `aria-hidden`, and both stop dead under
  `prefers-reduced-motion` — see the note in `assets/base.css` on why that is
  `animation: none` and not a shorter duration.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign b = block.settings

  comment
    ---- the mark ----

    The shared icon vocabulary: a source, a name off the theme's list, a size
    off the shared ladder. `icon-size` resolves the keyword against the theme's
    own icon settings, so Small here is the Small every other block means.
  endcomment
  capture icon_px
    render 'icon-size', size: b.icon_size, custom: b.icon_size_custom
  endcapture
  assign icon_size = icon_px | plus: 0

  assign icon_source = b.icon_source | default: 'icon'

  assign has_mark = false
  if icon_source == 'icon' and b.icon != blank and b.icon != 'none'
    assign has_mark = true
  elsif icon_source == 'image' and b.icon_image != blank
    assign has_mark = true
  endif

  comment
    ---- the person ----

    The ring is drawn at whatever size the portrait is, so only the portrait has
    a slider: the ring's own number is the gap between the two, which is the
    part a merchant can actually see and judge.

    `ring_span` is the outer diameter the layout has to reserve. It is computed
    here rather than in CSS because the stroke sits on the circle's edge and
    half of it falls outside — a ring drawn at exactly the reserved size would
    be clipped in half all the way round.
  endcomment
  assign avatar_size = b.avatar_size | default: 46 | plus: 0
  assign ring_style = b.ring_style | default: 'none'
  assign ring_width = b.ring_width | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign ring_gap = b.ring_gap | default: 0 | plus: 0

  assign has_ring = false
  if ring_style != 'none' and ring_width > 0
    assign has_ring = true
  endif

  assign ring_pad = ring_gap
  if has_ring
    assign ring_pad = ring_gap | plus: ring_width
  endif
  assign ring_span = avatar_size | plus: ring_pad | plus: ring_pad

  comment
    The circle is drawn in a viewBox measured in the same pixels the ring is
    rendered at, so one user unit is one CSS pixel and every number below is the
    number a merchant set. That is what keeps the dash pattern the same at every
    portrait size — in a normalised viewBox the dashes would stretch with the
    circle and a large portrait would come out with long dashes nobody asked
    for.

    The radius is the stroke's centre line, not its outer edge: half the stroke
    falls outside it, which is exactly the half the box has room for.
  endcomment
  assign ring_center = ring_span | divided_by: 2
  assign ring_radius = avatar_size | divided_by: 2 | plus: ring_gap

  case ring_style
    when 'dashed'
      assign ring_dash = '6 8'
    when 'dotted'
      assign ring_dash = '2 8'
    else
      assign ring_dash = 'none'
  endcase

  comment
    ---- the two loops ----

    The ring turns only when there is a ring to turn, and only when the merchant
    asked. A spin setting on a block whose ring is switched off is a control
    that does nothing, which is why this is an `and` and not two separate
    checkboxes the merchant has to keep in agreement.
  endcomment
  assign ring_spin = false
  if has_ring and b.ring_spin and b.ring_spin_duration > 0
    assign ring_spin = true
  endif

  assign avatar_zoom = false
  if b.avatar_zoom and b.avatar_zoom_scale > 0 and b.avatar_zoom_duration > 0
    assign avatar_zoom = true
  endif

  comment
    The zoom is a percentage in the editor because "grow by 6%" is a thing a
    merchant can picture and "scale to 1.06" is not. It reaches CSS as the
    multiplier `scale` actually takes.
  endcomment
  assign zoom_percent = b.avatar_zoom_scale | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign zoom_to = zoom_percent | plus: 100 | divided_by: 100.0

  assign connector_height = b.connector_height | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign has_connector = false
  if b.show_connector and connector_height > 0
    assign has_connector = true
  endif

  comment
    The portrait is never wider than the box it sits in, so the `sizes` hint is
    that number rather than a viewport fraction — the browser is told the one
    thing that is actually true about the box.
  endcomment
  assign avatar_sizes = avatar_size | append: 'px'

  assign has_person = false
  if b.avatar != blank or b.name != blank or b.role != blank or b.show_avatar
    assign has_person = true
  endif

  assign classes = 'expert-quote-lead'
  if ring_spin
    assign classes = classes | append: ' expert-quote-lead--spin'
  endif
  if avatar_zoom
    assign classes = classes | append: ' expert-quote-lead--zoom'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture block_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: b, declarations: true -%}
  --eql-measure: {{ b.quote_width | default: 880 }}px;
  --eql-quote-size: {{ b.quote_size | default: 28 }}px;
  --eql-quote-size-mobile: {{ b.quote_size_mobile | default: 20 }}px;
  --eql-mark-size: {{ icon_size }}px;
  --eql-mark-space: {{ b.icon_space | default: 0 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --eql-lead-space: {{ b.lead_space | default: 0 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --eql-connector-height: {{ connector_height }}px;
  --eql-connector-width: {{ b.connector_width | default: 1 }}px;
  --eql-avatar-size: {{ avatar_size }}px;
  --eql-ring-span: {{ ring_span }}px;
  --eql-name-size: {{ b.name_size | default: 20 }}px;
  --eql-role-size: {{ b.role_size | default: 13 }}px;
  {%- if b.icon_color != blank -%}
    --eql-mark-color: {{ b.icon_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if b.connector_color != blank -%}
    --eql-connector-color: {{ b.connector_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if ring_spin -%}
    --eql-spin-duration: {{ b.ring_spin_duration }}ms;
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if avatar_zoom -%}
    --eql-zoom-to: {{ zoom_to }};
    --eql-zoom-duration: {{ b.avatar_zoom_duration }}ms;
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<motion-effect
  class="{{ classes }}"
  data-block-spacing
  style="{{ block_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
  {% render 'motion-attrs', kind: 'text', block: b, children: true %}
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if has_mark -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Decorative. The quote underneath is the content, and a screen reader
      announcing "quotation mark" before reading a quotation is one wasting its
      user's time.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="expert-quote-lead__mark" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- if icon_source == 'image' -%}
        {% render 'image',
           image: b.icon_image,
           alt: '',
           ratio: 'adapt',
           sizes: '64px',
           wrapper_class: 'expert-quote-lead__mark-image' %}
      {%- else -%}
        {% render 'icon', icon: b.icon, size: icon_size, class: 'expert-quote-lead__mark-icon' %}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if b.quote != blank -%}
    <blockquote class="expert-quote-lead__quote rte">{{ b.quote }}</blockquote>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if has_person -%}
    <div class="expert-quote-lead__person">
      {%- if has_connector -%}
        <span class="expert-quote-lead__connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if b.show_avatar -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The portrait is announced by the name under it, so its own alt text is
          empty — "photo of Dr Adrian Sterling, Dr Adrian Sterling, Holistic
          Health Expert" is what the alternative sounds like. Same reasoning as
          `blocks/team-member.liquid`.

          `placeholder` so an unfilled block is a portrait-shaped box rather
          than a gap the merchant has to imagine the layout around.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="expert-quote-lead__portrait">
          {%- if has_ring -%}
            <span class="expert-quote-lead__ring" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 {{ ring_span }} {{ ring_span }}" fill="none" focusable="false">
                <circle
                  cx="{{ ring_center }}"
                  cy="{{ ring_center }}"
                  r="{{ ring_radius }}"
                  stroke="{{ b.ring_color | default: 'currentColor' }}"
                  stroke-width="{{ ring_width }}"
                  {% if ring_dash != 'none' %}stroke-dasharray="{{ ring_dash }}"{% endif %}
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                />
              </svg>
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}

          {% render 'image',
             image: b.avatar,
             alt: '',
             ratio: 'square',
             sizes: avatar_sizes,
             placeholder: 'hero-apparel-1',
             wrapper_class: 'expert-quote-lead__avatar' %}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if b.name != blank -%}
        <cite class="expert-quote-lead__name">{{ b.name }}</cite>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if b.role != blank -%}
        <span class="expert-quote-lead__role">{{ b.role }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</motion-effect>

